---
title: "06e  States of one contract, from award to closing"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  direction TB
  %% QUESTION THIS DIAGRAM ANSWERS: after the award, through which states does a contract pass, and which events remove it from the normal path?
  %% READING: the middle line is the normal path. The states on the sides are the exits and the returns. An arrow without text that returns to "In performance" means that the work continues.
  %% SHORT LABELS: "change agreed" = both parties agree to a variation or amendment within the legal limits. "allowed reason" = a reason for suspension or extension that the contract allows. "date passed" = the completion date passed, and liquidated damages are deducted from later payments. "legal ground" = default of the contractor or another ground for termination in the law.
  %% SOURCES: performance security before signing [RA12009 s.68]. Contract signing and notice to proceed [RA12009 s.66]. Warranty (retention money or bank guarantee for goods, repair of defects for works) [RA12009 s.90]. Blacklisting [RA12009 ss.98-105]. Multi-year contracts need a Multi-Year Contractual Authority, and payments may not exceed the cash appropriations of the year [GAA2026-GP][EO91]. Delivery must be inspected and accepted before the claim is due and demandable [JC2019-1].
  %% GENERAL KNOWLEDGE, NOT OPENED IN A SOURCE HERE: advance payment, progress billing, variation orders, suspension and extension of time, liquidated damages, termination. Their limits and percentages are in the Implementing Rules (GPPB Resolution No. 02-2025), which I did not open.

  state "Awarded" as AW
  state "Performance security provided" as PS
  state "Contract signed, obligation recorded" as SG
  state "Notice to proceed issued" as NTP
  state "In performance" as PERF
  state "Delivery or milestone claimed (billing)" as CL
  state "Inspected and accepted" as ACC
  state "Paid (partial or final)" as PAID
  state "Warranty period" as WAR
  state "Closed, securities released" as CLOSED
  state "Changed (variation or amendment)" as VAR
  state "Suspended, or time extended" as SUSP
  state "In delay, liquidated damages apply" as DELAY
  state "Terminated" as TERM
  state "Contractor blacklisted" as BL
  state "Rejected, to be corrected" as REJ

  [*] --> AW: head of the procuring entity issues the notice of award
  AW --> PS: winning bidder
  PS --> SG: head of the procuring entity and contractor, within 10 days from the notice of award
  SG --> NTP: within 3 days from approval of the contract
  NTP --> PERF: contractor starts
  PERF --> CL: contractor delivers or reports work accomplished
  CL --> ACC: inspection and acceptance by the agency
  CL --> REJ: delivery does not meet the contract
  REJ --> CL: contractor corrects
  ACC --> PAID: voucher, payment order (chapter 07)
  PAID --> PERF: more to deliver
  PAID --> WAR: final acceptance
  WAR --> CLOSED: no defect, or defects repaired
  PERF --> VAR: change agreed
  VAR --> PERF
  PERF --> SUSP: allowed reason
  SUSP --> PERF
  PERF --> DELAY: date passed
  DELAY --> CL: late delivery
  DELAY --> TERM: default
  PERF --> TERM: legal ground
  TERM --> BL: grounds proven
  WAR --> BL: defects not repaired
  CLOSED --> [*]
  TERM --> [*]
  BL --> [*]
